Z||000000||theogre||03-31-2000||11:42 PM||||I've recently gotten hold of a bunch of hard to find data. I will be working thru it and creating new documents to cover service for 87-88 Fiero that are not available in either Haynes or Chilton. (specifically details of DIS and the 700TBI) The data is nearly 1000 pages. It will take considerable time to absorb. The first result of it is the DIS how to in another thread.<P>I also have a complete RPO list for 87. (Too big to print for each year.) If you have checked the other RPO lists and cannot find all the codes post them here. <B>INCLUDE THE YEAR and ONLY the RPO codes you can't find in the other online lists.</B> some codes are year specific some aren't. I'll look in the 87 list and tell you what it says. I'm not even going to try every single year. (the 87 list is around 100 pages.)<P>There is also a bunch of stuff for the TH125. (Almost nothing for stick. sorry.) It turns out the TCC solinoid wasn't the only part of the TCC hang problem. (this problem can apply to all years.)<P>Warning: 87-88 4 cyl cars DO NOT use the same AC compressor as V6 and older 4 cyl cars. DO NOT service this system the same way as the older compressor. You Will screw up the system if you do.<P>Note: There are no recalls I could find other than the engine fire ones. All other documents you run into in that format are/were TSBs. TSBs cost money to fix. (I verified this at the <A HREF="http://www.nhtsa.gov/" TARGET=_blank>National Highway Traffic Safety Administration</A>)<P>AC recharge and R134a: GM does have approved methods for upgrade. I do not have all the documents, but the ones I do have confirmed some of what has been found on other sources. (like <A HREF="http://www.aircondition.com/" TARGET=_blank>Aircondition.com</A>) In short purge and blow out system, replace the ACC/dryer, replace orifice tube, dump oil from compressor if posible. Add new oil. Add new R134a to about 80-85% of the R12 volume.||||reg||1
